{"title":"Career roadmap — Teacher","role":"Teacher","summary":"A Teacher plans and delivers learning experiences, assesses student progress, supports individual learning needs and helps students develop academic, social and practical skills.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Education"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a BA Education graduate, the strongest career profile combines subject expertise + pedagogy + classroom management + educational technology + assessment + communication."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A BA alone may not qualify someone for every school-teaching position in India. Eligibility depends on the school level, subject, institution and applicable teacher-education/regulatory requirements. A B.Ed or another recognised teacher-education qualification is commonly important for school-teaching pathways."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build pedagogy, subject knowledge, classroom management, assessment and teaching-technology skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Establish expertise as a school/subject teacher and specialise in a subject, age group or teaching methodology"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Teacher, Academic Coordinator, Department Head or instructional-specialist roles"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move into school leadership, curriculum design, teacher training, education consulting or education entrepreneurship"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Education foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Child and adolescent development"},{"text":"Learning theories"},{"text":"Philosophy of education"},{"text":"Sociology of education"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Communication skills"},{"text":"Basic educational assessment"},{"text":"Classroom observation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Presentation skills"},{"text":"Empathy"},{"text":"Listening"},{"text":"Basic digital literacy"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Output","text":"Create lesson plans and conduct small peer-teaching sessions."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Teaching methodology"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pedagogical methods"},{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Questioning techniques"},{"text":"Activity-based learning"},{"text":"Differentiated instruction"},{"text":"Formative assessment"},{"text":"Summative assessment"},{"text":"Remedial teaching"},{"text":"Educational psychology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn digital tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Google Workspace/Microsoft 365"},{"text":"Interactive presentation tools"},{"text":"Learning Management Systems"},{"text":"Digital whiteboards"},{"text":"Online assessment tools"},{"text":"Basic educational content creation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Classroom specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Primary education"},{"text":"Secondary education"},{"text":"Special/inclusive education"},{"text":"Language teaching"},{"text":"Mathematics education"},{"text":"Science education"},{"text":"Social-science education"},{"text":"Educational technology"},{"text":"Early childhood education"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Curriculum mapping"},{"text":"Assessment design"},{"text":"Student progress tracking"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Individual learning plans"},{"text":"Classroom data analysis"},{"text":"Digital lesson design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-year projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong projects could include:"