":"h","text":"Recommended route"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Education","Teaching Internship","B.Ed/recognised teacher qualification","Teacher","Senior Teacher","Academic Coordinator","School Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"For an EdTech route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Education","EdTech + instructional design","Learning Content/Instructional Design role","Learning Designer","Learning Experience Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Study abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Strong areas"],"rows":[[{"text":"🇬🇧 UK"},{"text":"Education, TESOL, Educational Leadership"}],[{"text":"🇺🇸 USA"},{"text":"Education, Curriculum, Educational Psychology"}],[{"text":"🇨🇦 Canada"},{"text":"Education, Inclusive Education"}],[{"text":"🇦🇺 Australia"},{"text":"Education, Teaching, Educational Leadership"}],[{"text":"🇳🇿 New Zealand"},{"text":"Teacher Education, Inclusive Education"}],[{"text":"🇸🇬 Singapore"},{"text":"Education technology, curriculum and learning"}],[{"text":"🇫🇮 Finland"},{"text":"Education research and pedagogy"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful master's areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Curriculum & Instruction"},{"text":"Educational Leadership"},{"text":"Educational Technology"},{"text":"Inclusive Education"},{"text":"Special Education"},{"text":"Educational Psychology"},{"text":"TESOL/Language Education"},{"text":"Learning Sciences"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Teaching is often a regulated profession abroad. A foreign education degree does not automatically provide school-teaching eligibility; teacher registration, local qualifications and language requirements may apply."}]},{"heading":"Career progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Classroom pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Teaching Intern","Teaching Assistant","Teacher","Senior Teacher","Head of Department","Academic Coordinator","Vice Principal","Principal"]},{"type":"h","text":"Curriculum pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Teacher","Curriculum Developer","Curriculum Specialist","Academic Lead","Curriculum Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"EdTech pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Teacher","Content Developer","Instructional Designer","Learning Experience Designer","Learning Design Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Teacher-training pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Teacher","Mentor Teacher","Teacher Trainer","Professional Development Lead","Education Consultant"]},{"type":"note","label":"Emerging specialisations","text":"2030–2040"},{"type":"h","text":"1. AI-Enhanced Teaching"},{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Differentiated learning"},{"text":"Question generation"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Student practice"},{"text":"Learning analytics"},{"text":"Educational content creation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The teacher remains responsible for pedagogical judgement, student wellbeing, accuracy and ethical use of technology."},{"type":"h","text":"2. Personalised Learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Teachers will increasingly use student-learning data to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Knowledge gaps"},{"text":"Learning pace"},{"text":"Strengths"},{"text":"Areas requiring intervention"},{"text":"Individual learning pathways"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Learning Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Teachers and academic leaders will increasingly work with:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Student data","Learning patterns","Intervention","Outcome measurement"]},{"type":"p","text":"This makes basic data literacy increasingly valuable."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Inclusive Education"},{"type":"p","text":"Growing demand will exist for teachers who understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neurodiversity"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Learning difficulties"},{"text":"Universal Design for Learning"},{"text":"Assistive technologies"},{"text":"Differentiated instruction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Digital & Hybrid Education"},{"type":"p","text":"Teaching will increasingly combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classroom instruction"},{"text":"LMS platforms"},{"text":"Interactive content"},{"text":"Video"},{"text":"Simulations"},{"text":"AI tutors"},{"text":"Online assessments"},{"text":"Collaborative learning"}]},{"type":"note","label":"2040–2046","text":"How the role evolves"},{"type":"p","text":"The teacher's role will not disappear because of AI. Instead, routine information delivery will become easier to automate."},{"type":"p","text":"AI can increasingly handle:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic explanations"},{"text":"Practice questions"},{"text":"Automated feedback"},{"text":"Lesson-plan drafts"},{"text":"Learning-resource creation"},{"text":"Routine assessment analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Teachers will become increasingly valuable for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mentoring"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Critical thinking"},{"text":"Classroom culture"},{"text":"Social-emotional development"},{"text":"Complex explanation"},{"text":"Project-based learning"},{"text":"Ethical judgement"},{"text":"Personalised intervention"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The future teacher is therefore likely to function as a teacher + mentor + learning designer + learning-data interpreter."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Education"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Pedagogy"},{"text":"Curriculum design"},{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Inclusive education"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Teaching"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Activity-based learning"},{"text":"Differentiated instruction"},{"text":"Student mentoring"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Remedial teaching"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LMS"},{"text":"Digital classroom tools"},{"text":"Online assessment"},{"text":"Educational content creation"},{"text":"Learning analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted lesson planning"},{"text":"AI literacy"},{"text":"AI evaluation"},{"text":"Responsible AI in education"},{"text":"Personalised learning tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Conflict resolution"},{"text":"Collaboration"},{"text":"Continuous learning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Education + psychology + communication"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Pedagogy + lesson planning + assessment"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Classroom practice + digital teaching"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Teaching Assistant / Education Associate"}],[{"text":"Years 1–3"},{"text":"Teacher + subject/pedagogy specialisation"}],[{"text":"Years 3–6"},{"text":"Senior Teacher / Academic Specialist"}],[{"text":"Years 6–10"},{"text":"HOD / Academic Coordinator"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Principal / Academic Director / Education Consultant"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Education","recognised teacher-education qualification where required","strong subject knowledge","pedagogy","classroom experience","assessment skills","digital teaching","AI literacy","inclusive-education skills"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Key principle","text":"A strong teacher is not simply someone who knows a subject. The strongest educators can understand how students learn, design effective learning experiences, assess progress, adapt instruction, use technology responsibly and build an environment in which students can succeed."}]}]}